Requirements: 4   with obligations: 4

[task-01] When decomposition finds a span of the opening summary uncovered by the
    obligations already derived, and the follow-up call asked about that span alone
    returns neither an obligation nor an open question, the decomposition completes
    instead of stopping. The disagreement between the two steps is recorded as an open
    question on the summary requirement: it says that the two steps disagreed and quotes
    the span, and it links to the span's text in the task file. The rest of the
    decomposition, including every other span and requirement, is derived as usual.
    -> decomposition-completes  [functional/explicit]
       The decomposition completes instead of stopping.
    -> record-open-question-for-step-disagreement  [human_review/explicit]
       Record an open question on the summary requirement stating that the two steps
       disagreed and quoting the span.
    -> two-steps-disagreed  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Record that the two decomposition steps disagreed.
    -> quote-the-span  [docs_config/explicit]
       The requirement quotes the span.
    -> link-to-span-text  [functional/explicit]
       The open question links to the span's text in the task file.
    -> rest-of-decomposition-derived-as-usual  [invariant/explicit]
       The rest of the decomposition, including every other span and requirement, is
       derived as usual.
    ?  oq-01
       What should the decomposition do with the uncovered span when the follow-up call
       asked about that span alone returns neither an obligation nor an open question:
       should it complete and record the disagreement as an open question on the summary
       requirement, or should it stop?
    ?  task-01-span-01-disagreement
       The coverage step and the call asked about this span alone disagreed: the first
       found 'the follow-up call asked about that span alone returns neither an
       obligation nor an open question' uncovered by the obligations already derived,
       the second derived neither an obligation nor an open question from it. Does this
       span state a property of its own that must be delivered?

[task-02] A regression test is part of the deliverable: a replayed decomposition in
    which the follow-up call for an uncovered span yields nothing completes, and its
    result carries an open question quoting that span.
    -> replayed-decomposition-completes  [functional/explicit]
       A replayed decomposition in which the follow-up call for an uncovered span yields
       nothing completes.
    -> open-question-quote-span  [regression/explicit]
       Its result carries an open question quoting that span.

[exclusion-01] Do not change any prompt or response schema.
    -> prompt-response-schema-unchanged  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not alter any prompt or response schema.

[exclusion-02] The other refusals in the summary step (a span that is not part of the
    summary, a span decided more than once or not at all, a verdict that disagrees with
    its own counterexample) keep stopping the run.
    -> summary-step-refusals-stop-run  [invariant/explicit]
       The other refusals in the summary step continue to stop the run: a span that is
       not part of the summary, a span decided more than once or not at all, and a
       verdict that disagrees with its own counterexample.

